Loaded these 5 tools. Call them directly from now on, with input that matches the input_schema:
{"name":"bash_output","description":"Read a background command's output: whether it still runs, its exit code once it ended, and the output it printed since your last bash_output of it, or its last tail lines when tail is given. Output past the first 1 MB is kept from its end.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"The job id bash returned, such as bg-1."},"tail":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":1000,"description":"The number of last lines to return instead of the new output, such as 20."}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false}}
{"name":"monitor","description":"Watch a command's output and wake this session when a line matches pattern, when the command ends (you are told of its end as of any background command), or after timeout_s seconds (default 600, at most 3600). Give either command, which starts in the background as bash with run_in_background does, under the same approval and sandbox, or background_job_id to watch a command bash already started. It returns at once. End your turn while you wait: Geno starts your next turn with the matching line. Stop it with task_stop and the id it returns.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"A shell command to start in the background and watch, such as npm run dev."},"background_job_id":{"type":"string","description":"A running background command to watch, such as bg-1."},"pattern":{"type":"string","description":"A JavaScript regular expression matched against each new line of output, such as \"ready in \\\\d+ ms\"."},"timeout_s":{"type":"integer","description":"Seconds to watch before giving up, 600 by default, at most 3600."},"description":{"type":"string","description":"What the started command does, in 5 to 10 words, as for bash."}},"required":["pattern"],"additionalProperties":false}}
{"name":"list_agents","description":"List this session's subagents and background work, newest first: each subagent with its status (running, done, failed, cancelled, capped or interrupted), model, spend and age; each background command with its status and output file; and each pending monitor, wake-up and PR watch. Takes no input.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false}}
{"name":"task_stop","description":"Stop background work by the id it started with: a background command (bg-1), a monitor, wake-up or PR watch (wake-1), or a subagent running in the background (its session id). A command gets SIGTERM, then SIGKILL a few seconds later, and the result has the end of its output. A stopped monitor, wake-up or watch never wakes you. A stopped subagent's partial report is the result, with status cancelled, and no other report of it arrives. list_agents shows the ids.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"What to stop: bg-1, wake-1, or a subagent session id."}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false}}
{"name":"schedule_wakeup","description":"Wake this session after delay_s seconds (60 to 3600), such as to check CI again in 8 minutes. It returns at once and survives an engine restart. End your turn while you wait: Geno starts your next turn with reason. Do not schedule a short wake-up to poll for background work you started: Geno wakes you when a background command ends, a subagent reports or a monitor matches, so polling is wasted. Use it for work Geno cannot see, such as a deploy or a remote queue, with a delay matched to how fast that changes. Cancel one with task_stop and its id.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"delay_s":{"type":"integer","description":"Seconds from now, 60 to 3600."},"reason":{"type":"string","description":"What to do when you wake, in one line; you get it back then."}},"required":["delay_s","reason"],"additionalProperties":false}}

